{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And Jacob lived.</b> Rashi: this parashah is closed (setuma) because once he passed away, etc. And if you ask: but Yosef reigned after Jacob's passing? One may answer: when Jacob passed away, they began to enslave them little by little. Another interpretation: it is closed because the matter is connected to above, where he began to count the years of Jacob, and had not yet completed the reckoning until now." "<b>And Jacob lived in the land of Egypt.</b> But all his other years and life were not truly life, for all his days he was beset by grief; once he came to Egypt his spirit rested and he lived in tranquility. <b>In the land of Egypt, seventeen years.</b> This verse is written to Yosef's praise, that he provided for his father and all his household for seventeen years, just as his father had provided for him — for he was seventeen years old when he was sold."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:57.419370237Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}